plug.orion_install_confirm: "Orion is the part that loads plugins (DLL mods) into Stellaris. Installing it puts one file, winmm.dll, in the Stellaris folder:\n\n   {dir}\n\nWindows loads that file every time Stellaris starts. It does nothing in the Paradox Launcher, and it loads no plugin you haven't approved. Plugins run with the same permissions as you.\n\nYou can remove it any time from this page. Steam's \"verify files\" deletes it; Artemis puts it back the next time you launch."
plug.orion_is_installed: "Orion is installed."
plug.orion_up_to_date: "Orion is up to date."
plug.orion_remove_confirm: "Remove Orion? Stellaris goes back to starting without anything of ours, and no plugin loads. Your approvals and settings are kept."
plug.remove: "Remove"
plug.orion_removed: "Orion is removed."
plug.allow_build_confirm: "Orion has no verified data for this game build ({build}, {version}), so it loads no plugins here.\n\nIf you allow it, plugins that only use what Orion hands them (their settings, logging) will work. A plugin that changes the game's own code is on its own on a build nobody has checked, and can crash the game.\n\nThis applies to this exact build only; after a game update Artemis asks again."
